---
source: crates/engram-cli/tests/cli/snapshot/help.rs
expression: "f.run_bare(& [\"--help\"])"
---
$ engramdb --help
exit: 0
--- stdout ---
Project-scoped memory store for coding agents

Usage: engramdb [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init         Initialize a new EngramDB store
  add          Add a new memory
  get          Get a memory by ID
  query        Query memories (unified ranked / filtered retrieval)
  list         List all memories
  update       Update an existing memory
  delete       Delete a memory
  task         Task lifecycle: declare or complete the task this session works on
  verify       Confirm a memory is still accurate (stamps verified_at; clears doctor-flagged needs_review)
  config       Show effective config values, thresholds, and the store's top tags
  stats        Show statistics
  doctor       Check environment and store health
  projects     Manage registered EngramDB projects
  harvest      Inspect past Claude Code sessions for knowledge worth remembering
  groups       Manage multi-project memory groups and this project's subscriptions
  challenge    Challenge a memory's validity
  gc           Run garbage collection on low-relevance memories
  compress     List compression candidates (actual compression requires MCP mode)
  serve        Start the MCP server
  daemon       Run the shared embedding daemon (normally auto-spawned by MCP)
  completions  Generate shell completions
  migrate      Migrate memory files to the latest format version
  rollback     Roll back memory files to a previous format version
  reindex      Rebuild index and re-embed memories
  hook         Claude Code plugin hook handler
  setup        Set up Claude Code integration (hooks, MCP, ENGRAM.md, CLAUDE.md)
  review       Interactive review of challenged/stale memories
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - pretty: Human-friendly colored output with formatting
          - json:   JSON output for programmatic parsing
          - plain:  Plain text output without colors

      --json
          Output as JSON

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress non-essential output

  -v, --verbose
          Verbose output

      --no-color
          No colored output

      --dir <DIR>
          Working directory (default: current directory)

      --embedding-backend <EMBEDDING_BACKEND>
          Embedding backend: auto, onnx, or ollama

      --in-process
          Force in-process model loading — never contact the shared embedding daemon. Equivalent to setting ENGRAMDB_IN_PROCESS=1

      --spawn-daemon
          Spawn the shared embedding daemon if it is not already running, then route through it. By default the CLI only uses a daemon that is already running (connect-only)

      --no-maintenance
          Skip the automatic main-worktree maintenance pass (orphan-project cleanup + a quick store health check) for this invocation. Equivalent to setting ENGRAMDB_DISABLE_AUTO_MAINTENANCE=1

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
--- stderr ---
